        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: add publisher state facts",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Adds `specs/claim-official-state.md` for ClawHub claim, verification, official, suspension, and revocation state boundaries.\n- Adds derived publisher state facts for the existing official-publisher admin path: `claimState`, `officialState`, and `restrictionState` stay separate instead of collapsing into one trust badge.\n- Updates official-publisher add/remove audit metadata with prior and new official state, and extends the admin client schema to accept the optional state object while staying compatible with older server responses.\n\n## Trust boundary\n\nThis PR does not add self-service claim approval, verified state grants, follow state, profile UX, account-feed status fields, OpenClaw registry review, scan authority, install authority, or feed signing. `official` remains publisher-scoped and derived from ClawHub-managed `officialPublishers` rows only. Legacy personal publishers without `linkedUserId` derive claimed state from active owner membership compatibility rows.\n\n## Review follow-ups\n\n- `claimState` now requires active linked users or active membership users, so deleted/deactivated linked users or member rows do not make a publisher appear actively claimed.\n- Membership claim derivation uses bounded `by_publisher_and_role` role-bucket reads instead of unbounded collection scans on the official-publisher list path.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `git diff --check`\n- `git diff --cached --check`\n- `npx --yes oxfmt@0.56.0 --check convex/lib/publisherState.ts convex/lib/publisherState.test.ts convex/publishers.ts convex/publishers.test.ts packages/clawhub/src/schema/schemas.ts packages/clawhub/src/schema/schemas.test.ts specs/claim-official-state.md`\n- `rg -n \"Microsoft|micorosf|tenant|MOS3|M365|enterprise\" specs/claim-official-state.md convex/lib/publisherState.ts packages/clawhub/src/schema/schemas.ts` returned no matches\n- Final `codex review --base origin/main` reported no actionable findings after the active-user and bounded membership lookup fixes.\n- `bun --version` was not run successfully: `bun` is not installed in this Windows shell.\n- Targeted Vitest/tsc/Convex codegen were not run locally because this checkout has no `node_modules` and no local `vitest`, `tsc`, or `convex` binaries.",
